    "title": "pandas.Series.dt — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1661.gf74cda2e6e documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.dt#\n\n- Series.dt()[source]#\n- Accessor object for Series values’ datetime-like, timedelta and period properties. This accessor provides access to properties and methods for datetime-like, timedelta, and period data types. It can be used with Series containing datetime64, timedelta64, or period data. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **data** Series\n    - Series with datetime-like, timedelta, or period dtype.\n See also \n  - `DatetimeIndex`\n  - Index of datetime64 data.\n Examples >>> dates = pd.Series( ... [\"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-15\", \"2024-02-5\"], dtype=\"datetime64[ns]\" ... ) >>> dates.dt.day 0 1 1 15 2 5 dtype: int32 >>> dates.dt.month 0 1 1 1 2 2 dtype: int32 >>> dates = pd.Series( ... [\"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-15\", \"2024-02-5\"], dtype=\"datetime64[ns, UTC]\" ... ) >>> dates.dt.day 0 1 1 15 2 5 dtype: int32 >>> dates.dt.month 0 1 1 1 2 2 dtype: int32",
    "markdown_length": 864,
